speechtext:
Item agreed to.
Customs tariff-208. Boracie acid and borax in packages of not less than twenty-five pounds weight:	hydro-fluosilicic acid; tannic acid;
ammonia, sulphate of; cyanide of potassium; cyanide of sodium and cyanogen bromide; antimony salts, viz.: tartar emetic, chloride and lactate (antimonine); arsenous oxide; precipitate of copper (crude); verdigris or subacetate of copper, dry; sulphur and brimstone, crude or in roll or flour; argols; iodine, crude; bromine; sulphide of arsenic; carbon bisulphide: British preferential tariff, free; intermediate tariff, free; general tariff, free.

Item agreed to.
Customs tariff-525. Woven fabric, wholly of cotton, specially treated and glazed, when imported by rubber manufacturers for use, in their own factories, exclusively as a detachable protective covering for uncured rubber sheeting:	British preferential tariff, free;
intermediate tariff, 30 per cent; general tariff, 35 per cent.
